gavu(){return"Participation in live events and rehearsals"},
gauN(){return"How do I say I will not attend a live event or rehearsal?"},
gasP(){return"Open the project of the band that created the appointment, select the day and choose Opt out next to the live event or rehearsal. You will see You are not participating. If your plans change, choose Rejoin."},
gauP(){return"Can I choose even if I did not create the event?"},
gasU(){return"Yes. Each member can change their own participation in live events and rehearsals they can see in the project. This includes Limited members with access to the event. You cannot change someone else\u2019s choice."},
gauM(){return"If I opt out, does the event disappear or am I shown as free?"},
gasN(){return"The event stays in the calendar of the band that created it. In Personal mode, it no longer marks you as busy for that appointment: its list row shows a hollow dot and You are not participating. In Band mode, it keeps its color because the band\u2019s appointment still exists."},
gasO(){return"For example, you play in two bands and opt out of the first band\u2019s live event. In the second band\u2019s project, you will no longer be busy because of that event. Other commitments on the same day still count: opting out does not clear the whole day. Choose Rejoin to restore the commitment."},
gauL(){return"What does the small person icon in the calendar mean?"},
gasL(){return"It means you are not participating in at least one appointment of the band you are viewing on that day. The icon is at the bottom left: a soft green background means a live event and a soft blue background means a rehearsal."},
gauQ(){return"Do events I have declined appear in search?"},
gasW(){return"Yes. You can still find the event by searching the project of the band that created it, if you have permission to see it. Results show You are not participating. Details show Your participation separately from Confirmed or To be confirmed. Other projects no longer show the copy that marked you as busy for that event."},
gauO(){return"Does opting out change the event for other members?"},
gasR(){return"Your choice does not change the event, its confirmation or who can see it. You can therefore opt out even if the live event is already confirmed."},
gasS(){return"Choosing Opt out or Rejoin does not send other members a notification of your choice. It does not turn off notifications for you either: you may still receive event updates and project reminders according to the current rules and your preferences."},
gatb(){return"The owner manages groups in project settings. Tap the name in the Selected group panel to open the group list, with member counts and the default group indicator. The panel shows the active group\u2019s members and the button for adding more. Choose New group to create one, or use the menu beside its name to rename it or make it the default. Choose Save changes to apply your edits."},
gasm(){return"Use \xd7 to remove an address you have just entered; empty fields are ignored. You cannot invite yourself or add the same email twice to a group, even with different capitalization or spaces. If an address is incomplete, the app takes you to the field that needs correcting."},
gasK(){return"To hand ownership to someone else, choose Transfer ownership in the menu of a member with a confirmed account. Assigning the Admin role does not transfer ownership."},
gasQ(){return"The app initially treats you as participating: you do not need to confirm every appointment. You can change your choice for today and future dates. For past events, you can only view the choice already recorded."},
gasV(){return"The buttons are available in Personal and Band modes. If you are viewing a commitment from another band, open that band\u2019s project to change your choice. These buttons do not apply to personal unavailability."},
gasM(){return"The badge uses both colors if you have declined both live events and rehearsals on the same date. It does not mean the event is canceled or awaiting confirmation. This icon does not appear in other projects."},
gasT(){return"The Also visible to list is not updated by this choice: it shows explicit sharing with Limited members, not all participation responses from the band."},
gatE(){return"If the result is in the past, the app loads that month automatically. There is no need to open history first. Leaving search without choosing Show in calendar returns you to your previous view."},
gasY(){return"Dates follow Italian local time. Searching or loading the past shows entries that still exist; it does not recover deleted entries or previous versions."},
gasx(){return"In Personal mode and the calendar list, a question mark identifies tentative events. Search and details show Confirmed or To be confirmed. The colored person icon with You are not participating describes only your personal choice."},
